# Part 1 — Create a private Git repository for `hopestand-core-theme`

## Goal

Create a private online home for the code you write for your new custom HopeStand parent theme.

Your repository will contain:

```text
hopestand-core-theme/
```

It should **not** contain:

```text
WordPress core files
wp-config.php
passwords
API keys
payment keys
database exports
customer data
uploads
the original purchased theme, unless its license explicitly permits this use
```

A GitHub repository stores files and their revision history, and GitHub lets you choose private visibility when you create it. 

---

## Step 1.1 — Create or sign in to GitHub

1. Go to GitHub in your browser.
2. Create an account if you do not already have one.
3. Turn on multi-factor authentication for the account.
4. Choose a professional username you will be comfortable using long term.

Example:

```text
yourname
hopestand-dev
hope-stand
```

Avoid using a username that exposes unnecessary personal details.

---

## Step 1.2 — Create the repository

1. In GitHub, select the **+** icon in the upper-right corner.
2. Select **New repository**.
3. Enter these settings:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Owner | Your GitHub account |
| Repository name | `hopestand-core-theme` |
| Description | `Custom WordPress parent theme for HopeStand nonprofit and marketplace websites.` |
| Visibility | **Private** |
| Add a README file | Leave unchecked for now |
| Add .gitignore | Leave blank for now |
| Choose a license | Leave blank for now |

4. Select **Create repository**.

GitHub’s repository-creation workflow supports creating a repository from the web interface and selecting private visibility. 

5. Keep the GitHub page open. You will need the repository address shortly.

It will look similar to:

```text
https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/hopestand-core-theme.git
```

---

## Step 1.3 — Create your starter theme folder locally

Do this after you complete Part 2 and have LocalWP installed.

Inside your LocalWP site folder, you will eventually create:

```text
wp-content/
  themes/
