## Step 1.4 — Initialize Git and send your theme to GitHub

After you create the local theme folder and files:

1. In LocalWP, open your development site.
2. Right-click the site name.
3. Select **Open Site Shell**.
4. Navigate to your theme folder.

Your command will be similar to:

```bash
cd app/public/wp-content/themes/hopestand-core-theme
```

Local documents using **Open Site Shell**, navigating into `wp-content`, and initializing Git inside the theme directory when the repository is intended to track only a theme. 

5. Run these commands one at a time:

```bash
git init -b main
```

```bash
git add .
```

```bash
git commit -m "Initial HopeStand core theme structure"
```

6. Connect your local repository to GitHub. Replace `YOUR-USERNAME` with your GitHub username:

```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/hopestand-core-theme.git
```

7. Upload your code:

```bash
git push -u origin main
```

8. Refresh the GitHub repository page. You should see:

```text
style.css
functions.php
index.php
README.md
.gitignore
```

If Git asks you to identify yourself, use:

```bash
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"
```

Then repeat the commit and push commands.

